  "description_html": "<section aria-labelledby=\"courseDescription\">\n    Prerequisite: BIOL 1014 or higher level biology with laboratory.\n\nIntroductory course in plant diseases. A study of the causes, symptoms, spread and control of plant diseases. The emphasis is placed on the interaction between disease causing agents and the diseased plant and the way in which environmental conditions influence the mechanisms by which factors produce plant disease. \n\nLecture three hours, laboratory two hours.\n    \n</section>",
